hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1470","Muhammad bin Bashar narrated to us, Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, and Muhammad bin Jafar narrated to us, they said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada and Uqba bin Wasaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man’s prayer with all of them is superior to his prayer alone.” “With twenty-five,” Abu Bakr said: Abu Qudamah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Shu’bah, and something similar. Abu Bakr said: This word is of the type that I learned in the Book of Faith, that the Arabs may mention the number for a thing that has parts and branches without intending. Denying that the number exceeded that number, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not mean, when he said: “twenty-five,” that it is not preferred by more than This number is the evidence of the correctness of what I have interpreted."
"1471","Muhammad bin Bashar and Yahya bin Hakim told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed told us, Ubaid Allah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “A man’s prayer with all of them is superior to his prayer alone by twenty-seven degrees.” We are Bundar, we are Yahya, we are Ubayd Allah, Nafi’ informed me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
